-- title:
--   Unipotent inertia at primes q∤ M, q≠λ
-- statement:
--   Fix an integer $M\ge 1$, a prime $\lambda$ and a finite set $S$ of natural numbers, and let $O'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and with finite residue field, such that $\lambda$ lies in that maximal ideal. Let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism to $O'$ from the weight-two level-$M$ Hecke algebra away from $S$, i.e. from the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$ together with the operators $U_p$ for primes $p\mid M$ with $p\notin S$. Let $\rho$ be a [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) over $O'$: a free $O'$-module $V$ of rank two, finite over $O'$, with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\operatorname{End}_{O'}V$ which is adically continuous in the sense that for every $n$ there is a finite subextension $L/\mathbb Q$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\rho(\sigma)v-v\in \mathfrak m^n V$ for all $v\in V$ and all $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise. Assume that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid M$ and $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $\ell$ is a nonunit, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition group of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ and acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, one has $\operatorname{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\chi(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Then for every prime $q$ with $q\neq\lambda$ and $q\nmid M$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit and every $\sigma$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$, one has $\operatorname{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma))=(X-1)^2$.
--
--   This is the good-prime clause of the local behaviour of a two-dimensional $\lambda$-adic representation whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at almost all primes are those prescribed by a weight-two Hecke eigensystem of level $M$: at primes $q\nmid M$ away from the residue characteristic the inertia action has trivial semisimplification, which in particular holds for unramified representations. It is the companion, for primes not dividing the level, of the clause describing inertia at a prime exactly dividing the level, and is used in the analysis of characteristic polynomials on inertia attached to newforms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRepAdic_isUnipotentOnInertiaAt_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq_of_not_dvd.lean

